{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v6.json'))\nm['surfaces'].append(dict(entry_point='Async LocalAppendThread snapshot installation versus previously dispatched LocalApplyThread configuration entries',disposition='UNCLASSIFIED_PROTOCOL_RESPONSIBILITY',behavior_ids=['B-recovery','B-apply','B-membership'],reason='Local append and apply messages are independently scheduled under the documented asynchronous contract. Full restore installs snapshot ConfState; application messages already dispatched to a caller-owned queue are not revoked by raft. The in-repository interaction apply worker calls ApplyConfChange for every queued configuration entry without an index argument, whereas its append worker independently installs storage snapshots. The missing responsibility is how snapshot-covered application work must be reconciled: complete it before snapshot installation, discard covered entries, or otherwise prevent replaying historical configuration operations against restored membership. The acquired documentation does not specify this handoff. No production state-machine implementation or complete legal post-restore application history has been established for this Surface.',source_ids=['async-contract','async-worker-doc','storage-tail','snapshot-restore','config-activate','interaction-ready-routing','interaction-apply-worker','interaction-append-worker','interaction-snapshot-storage','rawnode-network-rejection'],high_consequence=True))\njson.dump(m,open('core-map-v6-surface.json','w'),indent=2)\ns=dict(action='research',rationale='Retain a reached producer prefix and the precise unresolved ownership contract without manufacturing a new obligation.',map_path='core-map-v6-surface.json',sources=[],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['1da528d106ac41228ed922e9d0f6aa2a','e10768b42d2a4a5ab01e2e0cdc2c974a','async-contract','async-worker-doc','snapshot-restore','interaction-apply-worker','interaction-append-worker','config-activate'],answered='The repaired exploration completed. Node 2 first retained a real MsgStorageApply containing joint-entry index 6 while committed=6 and applied=5. The other nodes left joint state and advanced the leader through applied index 10. The actual MemoryStorage snapshot producer returned index 10 with voters {1,2,3}; the lagging follower had last index 6. Actual leader replication emitted one MsgSnap. At the endpoint node 2 stored snapshot index 10, reported committed=applied=10, and still had exactly the original application batch at index 6 in its caller-owned queue. Thus matching-log fast-forward did not block this construction. The earlier removed-peer response error was a driver termination issue; its rejection was retained in the successful run. These observations are exploration, not property Evidence. The driver deliberately did not apply or discard the old batch, and the opaque snapshot data does not model external state-machine contents.',remaining=['No attributed rule yet determines caller handling of the snapshot-covered application batch; direct execution of an arbitrarily chosen policy would not resolve that applicability gap.','The new unclassified Surface retains the gap and its producer/consumer sources. A future check requires an applicable embedding contract or a narrower library-owned responsibility with an independent expectation.','Next research decision: compare the retained frontier and remaining source-grounded alternatives before spending the last experiment; do not treat available execution capacity as a reason to manufacture a disputed oracle.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Reachability is now answered by actual producers and a single execution history. Responsibility after that endpoint remains separate. Preserving the Surface avoids attributing an embedding policy to the core library or erasing a consequential gap merely because no formal Candidate is ready.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_10-41-34-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
